---
source: crates/zdk-cli/tests/auth_cli.rs
expression: "String::from_utf8_lossy(&auth.stdout)"
---
Log in and manage OAuth / API-token credentials

Usage: zdk auth [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  login    Log in: browser + PKCE (default), --client-credentials (CI) or --api-token (legacy)
  status   Show the active credential: grant, scopes, expiry countdown, store backend
  whoami   Show the signed-in user (GET /api/v2/users/me)
  refresh  Refresh (authorization code) or re-mint (client credentials) the access token now
  logout   Revoke the token server-side (best effort) and remove the stored credential
  test     One cheap call per product API the credential can reach
  token    Print the current access token — the only command that prints a secret
  scopes   Scope catalogue, presets and pre-flight checks

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Global options:
  -p, --profile <NAME>
          Profile (Zendesk instance) to target
          
          [env: ZENDESK_PROFILE=]

      --subdomain <SUB>
          Override the subdomain for this call (the `acme` in acme.zendesk.com)

  -o, --output <FORMAT>
          Output format (default: table on a terminal, json when piped)
          
          [possible values: table, json, ndjson, csv, tsv, yaml, raw]

      --fields <A,B,C>
          Keep only these fields (dot paths, comma-separated), e.g. id,subject,assignee.name

      --exclude <A,B>
          Drop these fields (dot paths, comma-separated)

      --compact
          Single-line JSON

      --jq <EXPR>
          Post-process with an embedded jq-compatible filter

      --all
          Auto-paginate to completion

      --limit <N>
          Stop after N records

      --page-size <N>
          Records per page (1-100)

      --sideload <A,B>
          Request sideloads, e.g. users,groups,comment_count

      --dry-run
          Print the request that would be sent and consume no quota

  -y, --yes
          Skip destructive-action confirmation

      --idempotency-key <KEY>
          Explicit Idempotency-Key for writes (auto-generated by default)

      --rate-limit-strategy <STRATEGY>
          What to do when a rate-limit budget is exhausted

          Possible values:
          - wait:  Sleep until the budget refills (default)
          - fail:  Exit 7 as soon as a budget is exhausted
          - burst: Skip the local governor; rely on 429 handling

      --max-concurrency <N>
          In-flight request ceiling

      --timeout <SECS>
          Per-request timeout in seconds

      --retries <N>
          Maximum attempts per request (overrides [retry].max_attempts)

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress non-error output on stderr (warnings, progress)

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase verbosity (-v info, -vv debug, -vvv trace with redacted request/response logs)

      --no-color
          Disable colour (NO_COLOR is also honoured)

      --audit-log <PATH>
          Append a structured NDJSON record of every API call to this file

      --config <PATH>
          Alternative config file (also ZENDESK_CONFIG)

      --credential-store <STORE>
          Where credentials are kept

          Possible values:
          - auto:    OS keyring when available, else the encrypted file
          - keyring
          - file
          - env:     Read-only: ZENDESK_ACCESS_TOKEN / ZENDESK_EMAIL + ZENDESK_API_TOKEN
          - none:    In-memory only (tests)

      --checkpoint <PATH>
          Write pagination progress to this file and resume from it
